WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.571
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:09.362
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:15.623
Unit thirty-one: So and Such (+ that). Today you will show the degree of something and its result.

4
00:00:15.923 --> 00:00:18.447
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.575
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:24.209
So.

7
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:28.238
So means to such a degree; used before an adjective.

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.165
It was so cold.

9
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.903
Your turn. Say: So.

10
00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:36.675
So.

11
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:38.209
Such.

12
00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:42.157
Such means used before an adjective + noun.

13
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.390
It was such a cold day.

14
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:47.218
Your turn. Say: Such.

15
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:50.963
Such.

16
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:52.799
So that.

17
00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:55.527
So that means in order that.

18
00:00:56.117 --> 00:00:58.256
I study so that I can pass.

19
00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.351
Your turn. Say: So that.

20
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.271
So that.

21
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:07.064
Such a.

22
00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.653
Such a means used before a singular noun.

23
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.611
Such a nice day.

24
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.625
Your turn. Say: Such a.

25
00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.328
Such a.

26
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:21.491
Result clause.

27
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:25.052
Result clause means the clause after that.

28
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.965
...that we stayed in.

29
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:30.667
Your turn. Say: Result clause.

30
00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:34.848
Result clause.

31
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:36.503
Degree.

32
00:01:37.517 --> 00:01:39.389
Degree means how much something is.

33
00:01:39.983 --> 00:01:41.251
A high degree.

34
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.945
Your turn. Say: Degree.

35
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.639
Degree.

36
00:01:48.383 --> 00:01:49.512
Adjective.

37
00:01:50.517 --> 00:01:53.143
Adjective means a word that describes a noun.

38
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.192
Cold is an adjective.

39
00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:57.948
Your turn. Say: Adjective.

40
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:01.871
Adjective.

41
00:02:02.617 --> 00:02:03.769
Noun phrase.

42
00:02:04.783 --> 00:02:07.851
Noun phrase means a noun with its describing words.

43
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:09.590
A cold day.

44
00:02:10.183 --> 00:02:12.789
Your turn. Say: Noun phrase.

45
00:02:15.633 --> 00:02:17.052
Noun phrase.

46
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:21.738
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:24.780
Visal, make a sentence with so…that.

48
00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:33.841
The soup was so hot that I couldn't eat it. So is followed by an adjective or adverb, and that introduces the result.

49
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:35.963
And such?

50
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:51.489
It was such a hot day that we stayed inside. Such is followed by a noun phrase: such a hot day, such delicious food. With plural or uncountable nouns we omit a: such good friends.

51
00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:53.956
Is that optional?

52
00:02:55.050 --> 00:03:08.328
In speech, that can be omitted. So that is different: it shows purpose, as in I study so that I can pass. Compare: so tired that I slept; such a tired day that I slept.

53
00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:11.048
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.883 --> 00:03:14.823
Grammar focus: So and such plus that.

55
00:03:15.123 --> 00:03:16.333
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.375
The soup was so hot that I couldn't eat it.

57
00:03:20.283 --> 00:03:22.794
It was such a hot day that we stayed inside.

58
00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:25.764
I study so that I can pass.

59
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:34.153
So + adjective / adverb. Such (a) + adjective + noun. Both + that + result. So that = purpose.

60
00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:38.208
Be careful! Don't say: It was so a hot day.

61
00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:42.306
Say: It was such a hot day.

62
00:03:42.606 --> 00:03:44.686
Use such before a noun phrase.

63
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.129
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:50.097
So Much That….

65
00:03:50.397 --> 00:03:52.640
The soup was so hot that I could not eat it.

66
00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.086
It was such a hot day that we stayed inside.

67
00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.319
She is such a kind person that everyone loves her.

68
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:04.204
I study every night so that I can pass the exam.

69
00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.979
The degree of heat was extreme.

70
00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:12.161
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.017 --> 00:04:15.272
The film was blank boring that I fell asleep.

72
00:04:15.572 --> 00:04:18.888
A, so. B, such. C, such a.

73
00:04:22.433 --> 00:04:24.236
The answer is A: so.

74
00:04:25.383 --> 00:04:27.801
It was blank a long road that we got tired.

75
00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:31.685
A, so. B, such. C, very.

76
00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:37.244
The answer is B: such.

77
00:04:38.383 --> 00:04:41.265
He speaks blank fast that nobody understands.

78
00:04:41.565 --> 00:04:45.126
A, so. B, such. C, such a.

79
00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:50.179
The answer is A: so.

80
00:04:51.317 --> 00:04:52.980
Which expresses purpose?

81
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:58.489
A, so that I can pass. B, so tired that I slept. C, such a day that.

82
00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:04.648
The answer is A: so that I can pass.

83
00:05:05.783 --> 00:05:09.385
According to the reading, why does the writer study every night?

84
00:05:09.685 --> 00:05:13.780
A, to pass the exam. B, for fun. C, for money.

85
00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:20.297
The answer is A: to pass the exam.

86
00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.733
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:28.825
Write one sentence with 'so…that' and one with 'such…that'.

88
00:05:37.617 --> 00:05:39.210
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:51.488
The test was so difficult that many students couldn't finish. It was such a long test that we needed three hours. I use so before an adjective and such before a noun phrase.

90
00:05:51.788 --> 00:05:53.741
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:58.579
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and so and such plus that.

92
00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:03.088
Today's value is analytical thinking. Look for the pattern underneath the surface.

93
00:06:03.388 --> 00:06:06.284
See you in Unit thirty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:06.584 --> 00:06:09.027
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

